# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GraveSigns environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
# The app runs in "demo mode" without Supabase (readings are still
# calculated and composed, just not stored).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anthropic (Claude) — REQUIRED to generate readings
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Models ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The reading runs SIX Claude passes. By default they are TIERED for latency so
# the request completes inside a serverless time limit:
#   • Composition (+ both rewrites) → Opus 4.8   — the family-facing reading
#   • The five ancillary passes     → Sonnet 5   — judgment, synthesis, ethics
#                                                   audit, verification, notes
# This keeps the prose at Opus grade while roughly halving the critical-path time.
#
# Overrides (later ones win):
#   ANTHROPIC_MODEL         → forces ALL passes to one model. Set it to
#                             claude-opus-4-8 to restore the all-Opus profile
#                             (slower — may exceed a 60s Hobby function limit).
#   ANTHROPIC_MODEL_AUX     → the default for the five ancillary passes.
#   ANTHROPIC_MODEL_<PASS>  → override a single pass (below).
#
# Model IDs: claude-opus-4-8  ·  claude-sonnet-5  ·  claude-haiku-4-5
#
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_AUX=claude-sonnet-5
#
# Per-pass overrides (defaults shown):
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_JUDGMENT=claude-sonnet-5      # Pass A — weigh the evidence
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_THEMES=claude-sonnet-5        # Pass S — the reading plan (themes + arc)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_COMPOSITION=claude-opus-4-8   # Pass B — the reading (+ all rewrites)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_ETHICS=claude-sonnet-5        # Pass E — ethical-alignment audit
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_VERIFICATION=claude-sonnet-5  # Pass C — fabrication audit
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_STUDY_NOTES=claude-sonnet-5   # Pass N — the practitioner's notebook

# Supabase — optional (enables saving & viewing previous readings)
# Project Settings → API in your Supabase dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Service role key — server-only, used by API routes to write readings
# with row-level security enabled. NEVER expose this to the browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
